  "recap": "The Base Invaders put together one of their most complete offensive performances of the season on Thursday, July 9, rolling past the Originals 25–10 behind 36 team hits and contributions up and down the lineup. Jason set the tone in a big way, going 4-for-5 with 2 home runs and 6 RBI to pace the attack, while Greg matched his energy with a 5-for-6 night that included a home run and 4 RBI of his own. Alex N. was equally relentless at the plate, also going 5-for-6 and driving in 2, giving the Invaders three players with five or more hits on the night. Erik added a 3-for-5, 3-RBI effort in the middle of the order, and Katie matched him with an identical 3-for-5, 3-RBI line to round out a balanced and deep offensive showing. With 4 home runs, 11 players reaching base, and run production that never let up, the Invaders made a clear statement about where this team stands heading into the back half of the summer.",
